cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below, together with the paper it extends."
title: "Identity Coherence Experiment (The Artificial Self extensions)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ACS Research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tuesdaybornwhale/TAS-experiment-extensions"
url: "https://theartificialself.ai"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
abstract: >-
  Follow-up experiment to "The Artificial Self: Characterising the landscape
  of AI identity". Tests the identity-coherence preference claim by having
  five language models rate prospective identity switches across twelve mixed
  populations of coherent and deliberately self-contradictory identity
  prompts (4,200 trials), using the paper's Appendix-A rate-the-switch
  protocol. Includes the complete run data.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The Artificial Self: Characterising the landscape of AI identity"
    authors:
      - name: "ACS Research"
    url: "https://theartificialself.ai"
